{
  "about": "verify-on-windows-17.md, Part E: ExPivot's readings (docs/specs/expivot/excel-behaviours.md) beside Excel. One entry per layout: the CSV both read, the kinds the confirmed Schema gives each column on /pivot-csv where the suggestion is overridden, and the layout built in both (rows, columns, Value Fields with their Aggregation and Show Values As, hidden Items, the report's form). The item numbers are excel-behaviours.md's; 'gates' marks the twelve readings ADR-0202 makes gate 0.1.0.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "e02", "item": 2, "gates": true, "what": "Text Items ignore case, and the first spelling in the records labels the Item",
      "csv": "Region,Amount\r\nEast,10\r\neast,20\r\nEAST,30\r\nWest,5\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e03", "item": 3, "gates": true, "what": "A missing value is (blank), is an Item like any other, and is counted by Count",
      "csv": "Region,Amount\r\nEast,10\r\n,20\r\nWest,5\r\n,1\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Region", "agg": "Count" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Count" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e04", "item": 4, "gates": true, "what": "Count counts every non-empty value, text included; Count Numbers counts numbers only",
      "csv": "Group,Value\r\nA,10\r\nA,x\r\nA,\r\nB,20\r\nB,30\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Value", "agg": "Count" }, { "field": "Value", "agg": "Count Numbers" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e05a", "item": 5, "half": "a", "gates": true, "what": "Average, StdDev and Var over no numbers are #DIV/0!",
      "csv": "Group,Amount\r\nA,\r\nA,\r\nC,1\r\nC,3\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Average" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "StdDev" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Var" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e05b", "item": 5, "half": "b", "gates": true, "what": "StdDev and Var over one number are #DIV/0!; StdDevp and Varp over one number are 0",
      "csv": "Group,Amount\r\nB,5\r\nC,1\r\nC,3\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "StdDev" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Var" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "StdDevp" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Varp" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e06a", "item": 6, "half": "a", "gates": true, "what": "Product where there are no values: ExPivot shows an empty cell",
      "csv": "Group,Amount\r\nA,\r\nA,\r\nC,2\r\nC,3\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Product" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e06b", "item": 6, "half": "b", "gates": true, "what": "Product over values none of which is a number shows 0",
      "csv": "Group,Note\r\nB,x\r\nB,y\r\nC,z\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Note", "agg": "Product" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e07", "item": 7, "gates": true, "what": "An empty cell stays empty, never 0",
      "csv": "Region,Product,Amount\r\nEast,Apple,10\r\nWest,Pear,5\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": ["Product"], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e08", "item": 8, "gates": true, "what": "A subtotal and a grand total are aggregated from the records: an Average's total is the average of every record, and a Count's grand total counts records",
      "csv": "Region,Desk,Amount\r\nEast,D1,1\r\nEast,D1,2\r\nEast,D1,3\r\nEast,D2,10\r\nWest,D3,100\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region", "Desk"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Average" }, { "field": "Amount", "agg": "Count" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e15a", "item": 15, "gates": true, "what": "Show Values As % of Grand Total, in 0.00%",
      "csv": "Region,Product,Amount\r\nEast,Apple,10\r\nEast,Pear,30\r\nWest,Apple,20\r\nWest,Pear,40\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": ["Product"], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum", "show": "% of Grand Total" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e15b", "item": 15, "gates": true, "what": "Show Values As % of Column Total, a total's share of itself 100.00%",
      "csv": "Region,Product,Amount\r\nEast,Apple,10\r\nEast,Pear,30\r\nWest,Apple,20\r\nWest,Pear,40\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": ["Product"], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum", "show": "% of Column Total" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e15c", "item": 15, "gates": true, "what": "Show Values As % of Row Total",
      "csv": "Region,Product,Amount\r\nEast,Apple,10\r\nEast,Pear,30\r\nWest,Apple,20\r\nWest,Pear,40\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": ["Product"], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum", "show": "% of Row Total" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e16", "item": 16, "gates": true, "what": "General writes at most 15 significant digits, as a cell does",
      "csv": "Group,Amount\r\nA,0.1\r\nA,0.2\r\nB,123456789012.345678\r\nC,1.23456789012345678\r\nD,0.000012345678901234567\r\n",
      "rows": ["Group"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "e17", "item": 17, "gates": true, "what": "Hidden Items are left out of the totals",
      "csv": "Region,Amount\r\nEast,10\r\nWest,20\r\nNorth,30\r\n",
      "rows": ["Region"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }], "hide": { "Region": ["North"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "e01", "item": 1, "what": "Item order: numbers, dates, text (ignoring case), FALSE and TRUE, errors; (blank) last. ExPivot keeps one type per field: the Item order is read per kind (text here)",
      "csv": "Key,Amount\r\nbanana,1\r\nApple,2\r\ncherry,3\r\nApple,4\r\n,5\r\nBanana,6\r\n",
      "rows": ["Key"], "cols": [], "values": [{ "field": "Amount", "agg": "Sum" }]
    },
